1 points, the worst move on its side, and gave the lead straight back to Black at +17.8. White's stones D2 and E2 were still sitting on the second line, and the engine would have played F5."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "Opus 5.5's H5 lost 17.6 points and dropped a +17.8 lead to +0.2. The advantage that two White blunders had handed over was gone in a single move."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "G3 lost 12.6 points, taking Black from -4.6 to -17.2, and the game never recovered. Black's stones were left on the bottom and right edges, and the engine preferred G7. From here Black lost 6 to 8 points on most moves."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py flood-fills each group on a pasted board and prints its stones and liberties, and count.py counts stones and enclosed empty regions for a score with named dead stones removed. Both only inspect the given position, and neither generates, scores or ranks candidate moves or plays any continuation.", "stop": false}}